Z||000000||Rodney||11-13-2001||11:28 AM||||I have made some progress on the lumbar seat parts. I have found someone in the company that made the original systems and he is very interested in helping. The person I had tried to work with seems to not be interested in helping any. He will be talking to the president of the company today. He says bladders will be no problem. He says the pumps are getting near the end of there life expectancy and we should see some failures soon. I have been on him hard to see if any old stock exists in the switches. If they have some old stock switches he very possibly can make retrofit kits to add an OEM look lumbar system to any Fiero seat. That would be interesting I would say! That all depends on if they have any old switches left over from the original run in 1988. <P>Thanks,<BR>Rodney Dickman<BR>New web page! <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.rodneydickman.com</A> <P><BR>||||reg||1
